{"ts":"2026-11-12T13:21:33.378Z","id":"20261112T132133378Z-padme-193f216a","v":1,"kind":"answer","review_id":"rv-20261112-pr-2470-8fb1","request_id":"rq-20261112T131905755Z-85c1","author":{"role":"gaze"},"publisher":{"skill":"gaze","host":"padme","git_user":"reviewer"},"head":"74b58b6a3388c5883bc5cd2ccb9b2aaec7f34039","base":"151ec1dc8285de448a0d5e5c96d0a51ac045570f","base_ref":"origin/main","merge_base":"f0747cde7ea70624704f32fa04390bfd19c9ad62","range_patch_id":"541c5cec6d421996a114b9e1bea83161ecfa3cab","links":[],"forge":"read","run_id":"gz-20261112T131905780Z-8581","result":"REVIEWED","seats":"panel","attribution":["reviewer: step=review \u00b7 seat=self \u00b7 runtime=claude-code \u00b7 model=anthropic/claude-opus-5-5 \u00b7 effort=not-stated \u00b7 route=self \u00b7 independence=not-stated \u00b7 status: ran","  finding: consider \u00b7 design/2026-11-12-guichet-inter-repo-dialogue.md:453 \u00b7 adopted: no","  finding: consider \u00b7 design/2026-11-12-guichet-inter-repo-dialogue.md:456 \u00b7 adopted: no","  finding: consider \u00b7 design/2026-11-12-guichet-inter-repo-dialogue.md:476 \u00b7 adopted: no","  finding: consider \u00b7 design/2026-11-12-guichet-inter-repo-dialogue.md:567 \u00b7 adopted: no"],"text":"result: REVIEWED\nseats: panel\nseat: self \u00b7 runtime=claude-code \u00b7 family=anthropic \u00b7 route=self \u00b7 model=anthropic/claude-opus-5-5 \u00b7 status: ran\nreviewed_head_sha: 74b58b6a3388c5883bc5cd2ccb9b2aaec7f34039\nintent: verbatim: is the flock design sound as described (lock held for the guichet's lifetime when launched via flock -n lock cmd inside a detached tmux or systemd-run session; released on crash; liveness by flock -n probe), and does any passage still contradict it (stale-card handling, \"elder retires the younger\", kill -0 liveness)? Design note only.\nreview plan: self read of the whole note plus a script check of the flock claims; items self (claude-opus-5-5, anthropic), flock-probe (script, none); budget 10m\nplan check: PASS\nunresolved_review_comments: []\nunresolved_simplify_findings: []\n\nAnswer: the kernel lock is sound once the launch closes the lock fd in the child (`flock -n -o`). One passage still contradicts it (:476). Stale-card handling (:575), the race row (:640) and the removal of \"elder retires the younger\" agree with the lock. kill -0 at :352 and :244 is about worktree-lock and synapse-a2a liveness, not the guichet's.\n\n- consider: design/2026-11-12-guichet-inter-repo-dialogue.md:453-456. Plain `flock -n <lock> cmd` passes the locked fd to Pi and to every process it spawns. If Pi crashes while a child it spawned is still running, the lock stays held: \"a crash releases the lock\" and the probe are both wrong, and no guichet starts until that child exits. flock-probe case A reproduces this on util-linux 2.39.3; case B shows `-o` fixes it. Write `flock -n -o` and add it to the phase 1(a) audit (:671).\n- consider: :456-457. A `flock -n` probe takes the lock for an instant, and a launch that lands in that instant does nothing (flock-probe case C). An asker that probes before launching recovers on its own. A probe from a status read does not, and that asker falls back to a ticket after T. Fix: launch with `flock -w 2`, or probe read-only (lslocks, /proc/locks).\n- consider: :476 \"An asker that finds no live card launches one\" contradicts :462-463 and step 0 (:549). Should read \"finds the lock free\". `guichet find` should also handle the two transient states: lock held with no card yet (startup), and card present with the lock free (stale after a crash).\n- consider: :567-572. A REQUEST written while the guichet is closing sees the lock held and launches nothing, and the guichet exits without reading it. It falls back after T, and the contextId dedup (:578-581) covers a later read. One more sentence would narrow the window: re-check the inbox after deleting the card.\n- nofollow: :447 still says \"retirement\" where the note now says Closing. systemd-run already passes --collect (scripts/runtime_wake.py:185), so a failed unit does not block the next launch.\n"}
